Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using inverse error on the full pool to see if weighting improves over the mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on the full pool to see if it improves over mean and weighted.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean on the full pool to see if trimming outliers improves over median.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a dba combination on the full pool to see if it improves over trimmed_mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool_full","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using the pooled_meta_model handle on the full pool to see if that improves over inverse_error weighting.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w1"}

Thought: Test a single best model (ARIMA) to see if a single strong model beats the robust combinations.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"ARIMA"}

Thought: Test a simple mean on a smaller, more relevant pool to see if reducing model set improves robustness.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the smaller, more relevant pool1 using inverse_error weights to see if weighting improves over simple mean on that pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on the smaller, relevant pool1 to see if it outperforms trimmed_mean on full pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean on the smaller, more relevant pool1 to see if trimming improves over the current trimmed_mean on full pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool1","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on a new, slightly larger pool (pool2) using inverse_error to see if expanding the pool improves over trimmed_mean full.  

Action: evaluate_strategy  

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"inverse_error"}

